OWNER SESSION (throwaway box; no real secret reused)
  - users table was empty. Seeded owner row + business_profile row directly
    in the droplet DB (same shape as the repo fixture in
    tests/browser/owner-session.ts / tests/helpers/performance-browser.ts):
      users:  id 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,
              email owner@example.test, role owner,
              password_hash scrypt(N=16384,r=8,p=1) of throwaway passphrase
              "PerfOwnerPassphrase-2026!" (generated locally with the app's
              exact src/core/auth/passwords.ts parameters)
      business_profile: id 1, 'Perf Studio', CA/CAD, America/Vancouver,
              setup_completed_at now()
  - HTTP setup of the droplet blocks registerOwner (NODE_ENV=production,
    BOOTSTRAP_SECRET unset), so the documented seed path was used and the
    session itself was established through the app's REAL login over HTTP:
      1. POST /api/auth/login {email,password} -> 200, session cookie
         (twoFactorRequired:false at that point — no factors yet)
      2. Privileged roles must enroll 2FA (guard redirects to
         /security?required=1), so TOTP was enrolled through the real
         services over HTTP:
           POST /api/v1/auth.beginTotpEnrollment -> {enrollmentToken, secret}
           TOTP code computed locally (HMAC-SHA1/30s/6-digit, same algorithm
           as src/core/auth/two-factor-crypto.ts)
           POST /api/v1/auth.confirmTotpEnrollment -> ok:true, factor live
      3. Session cookie now passes the admin gate (verified /admin/contacts
         -> 200).
  - All measured admin/editor requests carry this real login session cookie.

